From 5e8c4faa9aa772f7af9d50cb7e02c547106faa35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hgi586 <154084457+hgi586@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:35:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sdr): sweep SoapySDR devices

Add a SoapySDR backend to the SDR Sweep block so radios without a native
driver, such as the USRP B200 family through SoapyUHD, can sweep wide
bands. Each hop retunes and captures one burst, so no sample predates the
retune; drivers without burst support restart the stream at each hop.

UHD only reports the rates of the current master clock, so the backend
probes common higher rates and widens the capture rate range when the
driver accepts one. Drivers with a native backend are left to it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
